### Tutorial case: the two-dimensional heat equation.
###
###   u_t = a ( u_xx + u_yy ),   a = 0.05,   on (0,1)^2 x (0, 0.1]
###   u* = exp(-2 a pi^2 t) sin(pi x) sin(pi y)
###
### Three input variables in the order (x, y, t), so D0 = 3 and the time
### axis is the last one, which is the default Time_axis.  Written as a
### residual that must vanish:
###
###   R = u_t - a u_xx - a u_yy = 0
###
### The multi-index of a term counts how many times each variable is
### differentiated, in the order the layer widths are given:
###
###   u_t    -> (0 0 1)      one derivative in t
###   u_xx   -> (2 0 0)      two derivatives in x
###   u_yy   -> (0 2 0)      two derivatives in y
###
### See docs/TUTORIAL.md for the reasoning behind every line below.
Init_w       Glorot_norm
Rand_seed    20260731 / fixed seed, so the run is reproducible
Restart      0 /
Output_deriv 0 /

Nlayer       4 / L
3 / ndim(1) = D0 = number of input variables (x, y, t)
24 /
24 /
1 / ndim(L) must be 1

Loss_term  DATA         440  data.dat    1.d0  / initial condition and walls
Loss_term  COLLOCATION  600  colloc.dat  1.d-1 / interior, where R = 0 is imposed

Residual 3 /
LIN   1.d0     0 0 1 /   u_t
LIN  -0.05d0   2 0 0 /   -a u_xx
LIN  -0.05d0   0 2 0 /   -a u_yy
Exact_solution 1 /       colloc.dat carries u* in its last column

Hod_K      2 /   the residual needs second derivatives, so K = 2
1.d0             lambda_0, on the value
0.d0             lambda_1, unused here
0.d0             lambda_2, unused here
Hod_dense  0 /   carry the closure of the residual indices, not the dense set

Hod_check  1 /   verify the gradient against finite differences before fitting

Num_validation 60 /
Validation_cyc 200 /
P_max          500 /
Epoch      6000 /
Conv       1.d-12 /
Num_batch  40 /
Checkpoint_cyc 100000 /
Activation TANH /
GD_method  Adam
GD_param   0.004d0 0.9d0 0.999d0 1.d-8 0.d0 /
